WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.680
Everyone has had something to say about fat
Thor in Avengers: Endgame, and now Robert

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.540
Downey Jr. has added his two cents.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:11.280
Chatting with Variety as part of the outlet's
cover story all about Thor himself, Chris

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.760
Hemsworth, Downey Jr. spoke out about the
God of Thunder's striking new physique.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:17.160
"Thor!"

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.120
"Is he asleep?"

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.939
The five years after the Avengers' post-Infinity
War face-off with Thanos, which ended with

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.940
Thor decapitating the tyrant, weren't kind
to the God of Thunder.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.800
The mighty Asgardian sank into a pit of grief
isolating himself to a small shack in New

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.399
Asgard and spending his days eating, drinking,
and yelling at kids while playing Fortnite.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:40.500
He emerged after the time jump sporting a
shaggy beard, unkempt hair that grew to his

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.820
shoulders, and a protruding belly courtesy
of barrels of beer and newfound love for Cheez

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.320
Whiz.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.120
Chubby Thor divided fans, but where does the
Iron Man actor sit on the spectrum?

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.550
Downey Jr. revealed to Variety that he adores
what Hemsworth did with the character, and

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.400
praised his all-or-nothing performance.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.899
"Boy, did he go bonkers.

00:00:56.899 --> 00:00:58.320
He went out to the bleeding edge.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.429
I have a rule, which is if you think you're
at 70 percent, then start pulling back, because

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.380
it's probably at 105 [percent].

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.580
He went out into some pretty risky atmosphere
of nuttiness."

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.800
"I think I'm having a panic attack."

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:09.980
"Get it together!"

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.080
Hemsworth relished the experience of pushing
himself to his limits and continuing to take

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.160
risks with Thor.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.510
In fact, Hemsworth was so excited about being
able to play Thor in a different way and enjoyed

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:24.720
chubbier Thor so much that he pushed to keep
the hero's plumper shape throughout the entirety

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.080
of Endgame, lobbying to not have Thor undergo
the planned mid-movie transformation where

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:29.860
he gets fit again.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:30.940
He told Variety,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.360
"I like that anything goes.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.060
You're not locked into expectations.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.600
I enjoyed that version of Thor.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.460
It
was so different than any other way I played

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.240
the character.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.400
And then it took on a life of its own."

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.100
"Give me that.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:41.040
You have the little one."

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.520
Hemsworth even found some joy in the not-so-fun
parts of portraying fat Thor, namely the heavy

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.660
silicone prosthetics and extra weights he
had to wear, saying,

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.570
"Physically, it was a good three hours in
hair and makeup.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:56.610
Then the prosthetic suit, particularly for
the shirt-off scene, that was a big silicone

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.170
that weighed about 90 pounds.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.360
It was certainly exhausting.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.140
I had weights on my hands and ankles just
to have my arms and legs swing differently

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.860
when I shuffled along through the set.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.420
People just kept coming up and cuddling me
like a big bear or rubbing my belly like I

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.100
was pregnant.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.760
Or trying to sit on my lap like I was Santa
Claus.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.760
You get a lot of affection.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.840
I felt like an old man, an old grandpa, with
a bunch of kids around."

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.110
Downey Jr. wasn't the only Endgame guy who
had kind words to say about chubby Thor.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.340
The film's co-director, Anthony Russo, shared
with Variety that Thor's arc in Endgame was

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.460
among his favorite narratives in the entire
film.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.720
Like Downey Jr., Russo also applauded Hemsworth's
commitment to his character.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.160
"Part of Chris' magic as a comedic actor is
his dedication to the depth of the character

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.069
on a very earnest level...It's so devious
and subversive when comedy is coming from

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:42.000
a place of complete commitment and emotional
complexity."

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.880
While those over in the Marvel camp clearly
couldn't get enough of fat Thor, others were

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.640
less keen on the character's new look.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.180
His transformation from fit to fat, largely
due to the trauma of the Decimation and the

00:02:52.181 --> 00:02:56.450
subsequent grief Thor struggled to work through,
didn't sit well with some viewers, many of

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.590
whom felt that Avengers: Endgame was poking
fun at his troubles rather than celebrating

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.140
him in the way they felt the film was doing
with other heroes.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.880
At the end of the day, though, it looks like
fat Thor is here to stay, as Hemsworth has

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:10.060
no desire to exit the Marvel Cinematic Universe
any time soon.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.620
"I'd still love to do more, to be honest.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.960
And I don't know what the plan is.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.300
I feel like we've opened up such a different
character.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.000
I feel more energized for the possibility
of where it could go."

